@startuml
title Deadlock Playground - Use Case Diagram

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #444444
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontColor #222222
}

skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
  ArrowColor #444444
}

actor "User\n(Student / Instructor)" as User

rectangle "Deadlock Visualisation and Recovery Simulator" {

  usecase "UC1: Configure\nScenario" as UC1

  usecase "UC2: Request\nResource" as UC2

  usecase "UC3: Release\nResource" as UC3

  usecase "UC4: Step Through\nSimulation" as UC4

  usecase "UC5: Detect\nDeadlock" as UC5

  usecase "UC6: Recover\nfrom Deadlock" as UC6

  usecase "UC7: Reset\nScenario" as UC7

  usecase "Preempt Resource\n(Recovery Option)" as PRE

  ' Encourage a logical vertical arrangement

  UC1 -[hidden]down-> UC2
  UC2 -[hidden]down-> UC3
  UC3 -[hidden]down-> UC4
  UC4 -[hidden]down-> UC5
  UC5 -[hidden]down-> UC6
  UC6 -[hidden]down-> UC7
}

' --------------------------------
' Actor associations
' --------------------------------

User --> UC1

User --> UC2

User --> UC3

User --> UC4

User --> UC5

User --> UC6

User --> UC7

' --------------------------------
' Use case relationships
' --------------------------------

UC6 ..> UC5 : <<include>>

PRE ..> UC6 : <<extend>>

' --------------------------------
' Use case notes
' --------------------------------

note right of UC1
  Configure processes, priorities,
  resources, instance counts,
  shareability and operations.

  Select prevention settings and
  optional Banker's avoidance.

  Textbook presets are not
  implemented.
end note

note right of UC2
  Requests can be granted,
  blocked, denied as unsafe,
  or rejected by prevention.

  Banker's safety checking applies
  only when avoidance is enabled.

  Demo mode permits unsafe grants.
end note

note right of UC4
  Step executes scheduled operations.

  Hold and Wait prevention may
  require atomic request groups.

  Event History separately supports
  backward and forward navigation.
end note

note right of UC5
  Single-instance configurations
  use cycle detection.

  Multi-instance configurations
  use Banker's-style detection.

  A structural cycle does not
  always prove deadlock.
end note

note right of UC6
  Recovery uses one of three
  victim-selection policies:

  Priority
  Resources Held
  Recovery Cost

  Terminate and Preempt are
  alternative recovery strategies.

  Multiple rounds may be needed.
  Recovery may remain unresolved.
end note

note right of UC7
  Reset clears the current
  browser session's scenario.

  Processes, resources, graph
  and event history return
  to their unconfigured state.

  Other sessions are unaffected.
end note

note bottom of PRE
  Extension condition:
  The user selects PREEMPT
  as the recovery strategy.

  Termination is the other
  supported recovery strategy.
end note

legend bottom
  USE CASE RELATIONSHIPS

  User associations:
  The student or instructor can invoke
  the seven primary use cases.

  <<include>>:
  Recovery uses deadlock detection
  internally. The user does not need
  to invoke Detect separately.

  <<extend>>:
  Preemption is an optional recovery
  behavior selected by the user.

  Banker's avoidance:
  Conditional behavior within resource
  requests and scheduled execution,
  not an unconditional included use case.

  Event-history navigation:
  Supporting interaction within the
  simulation interface.

  Sessions:
  Each browser session operates on
  its own temporary simulation state.
endlegend

@enduml
